## 🗓️ Running It as a Workshop

| Time | Activity | Output |
|------|----------|--------|
| Pre-work | Request the AI inventory and one completed impact assessment | Reality check before anyone speaks |
| 0:00–0:10 | Frame the 74%/27% gap. Name the goal as calibration, not grading | Permission to score honestly |
| 0:10–1:10 | Score D1–D8 on the Assessment tab. **Evidence or it didn't happen** | Scored baseline with evidence references |
| 1:10–1:25 | Read the Results tab; work the failed gates first | List of deployments that should pause |
| 1:25–1:45 | Set 12-month targets per domain | Defensible target profile |
| 1:45–2:00 | Read the Roadmap tab's top two by weighted gap | Q1 focus with named owners |

**Two facilitation notes earned the hard way in the model's design:**

The pre-work request does more diagnostic work than the first hour of discussion. The gap between the inventory that arrives and the inventory people describe in the room is your most honest signal, and you get it for free.

And don't let the room target L5 everywhere. Outside D2 and D6, L4 is usually the right twelve-month ceiling — L5 implies a self-tuning control loop that most programs cannot staff, and an unreachable target is indistinguishable from no target.

